# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and runs on Linux in
# Docker. Left alone, git checks shell scripts out with CRLF line endings, and
# a script whose shebang line ends in \r fails inside the container with:
#
#   exec /opt/backup/backup.sh: no such file or directory
#
# which points at the file, not at the invisible carriage return that's
# actually the problem. Pinning LF for everything the container executes means
# the same bytes exist on Windows, on Linux, and in the image.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.dump binary
